  "warnings": [
    "Check hepatitis B status before starting rituximab. Positive serology requires liver disease specialist consultation. Active HBV infection is a contraindication.",
    "Rituximab is associated with cytokine release syndrome (CRS) — occurs most commonly within 1-2 hours of first infusion. Monitor for severe dyspnoea, bronchospasm, hypoxia, fever, chills, urticaria, angioedema.",
    "Rituximab is associated with risk of progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML). Monitor for neurological, cognitive, or psychiatric symptoms.",
    "Vincristine MAXIMUM DOSE 2mg regardless of BSA — vincristine overdose causes permanent paralysis and death.",
    "Vincristine is a vesicant — NPSA/2008/RRR04 must be followed for IV vinca alkaloid administration.",
    "Cyclophosphamide may cause haemorrhagic cystitis (rare). Consider mesna in patients with pre-existing bladder disorders.",
    "Assess for cold or flu-like symptoms prior to rituximab — viral URTI increases risk of severe infusion reaction.",
    "Consider gastric protection with PPI or H2 antagonist in high-risk patients receiving prednisolone.",
    "Consider pethidine 25-50mg IV for rituximab-related rigors not responding to steroids."
